<article class="env-lemma" id="05N2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05N2">Lemma <span data-tag="05N2">3.7.1</span>.</a> Suppose that $T = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{\alpha < \beta } T_\alpha $ is a colimit of sets indexed by ordinals less than a given ordinal $\beta $. Suppose that $\varphi : S \to T$ is a map of sets. Then $\varphi $ lifts to a map into $T_\alpha $ for some $\alpha < \beta $ provided that $\beta $ is not a limit of ordinals indexed by $S$, in other words, if $\beta $ is an ordinal with $\text{cf}(\beta ) > |S|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For each element $s \in S$ pick a $\alpha _ s < \beta $ and an element $t_ s \in T_{\alpha _ s}$ which maps to $\varphi (s)$ in $T$. By assumption $\alpha = \sup _{s \in S} \alpha _ s$ is strictly smaller than $\beta $. Hence the map $\varphi _\alpha : S \to T_\alpha $ which assigns to $s$ the image of $t_ s$ in $T_\alpha $ is a solution. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>